              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="seo/"><strong>SEO</strong></a> — Search Engine Optimization</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="local-seo/"><strong>Local SEO</strong></a> — for businesses serving a specific geography</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="technical-seo/"><strong>Technical SEO</strong></a> — the engineering side of SEO</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="ppc/"><strong>PPC</strong></a> — Pay-Per-Click advertising</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="cpc/"><strong>CPC</strong></a> — Cost Per Click</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="cpa/"><strong>CPA</strong></a> — Cost Per Acquisition / Action</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="roas/"><strong>ROAS</strong></a> — Return on Ad Spend</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="ctr/"><strong>CTR</strong></a> — Click-Through Rate</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="conversion-rate-optimization/"><strong>CRO</strong></a> — Conversion Rate Optimization</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="landing-page/"><strong>Landing Page</strong></a> — a standalone page built for a single campaign</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="retargeting/"><strong>Retargeting</strong></a> — ads shown to people who already visited</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="lookalike-audience/"><strong>Lookalike Audience</strong></a> — Meta and Google audience expansion</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="marketing-funnel/"><strong>Marketing Funnel</strong></a> — awareness → consideration → conversion → retention</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="lead-magnet/"><strong>Lead Magnet</strong></a> — a free resource that captures contact info</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="utm-tracking/"><strong>UTM Tracking</strong></a> — parameters for attributing traffic sources</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="backlink/"><strong>Backlink</strong></a> — A link from another website to yours; a core signal of authority in search.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="domain-authority/"><strong>Domain Authority</strong></a> — A third-party score predicting ranking strength (not a Google metric).</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="serp/"><strong>SERP</strong></a> — The Search Engine Results Page — organic results, ads, the map pack, and AI overviews.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="organic-traffic/"><strong>Organic Traffic</strong></a> — Unpaid visitors who arrive from search results.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="customer-lifetime-value/"><strong>Customer Lifetime Value (LTV)</strong></a> — The total revenue you expect from one customer over the whole relationship.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="quality-score/"><strong>Quality Score</strong></a> — Google Ads' 1-10 rating of ad and landing-page relevance that lowers your costs.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="attribution-model/"><strong>Attribution Model</strong></a> — The rule that decides which touchpoints get credit for a conversion.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="featured-snippet/"><strong>Featured Snippet</strong></a> — The answer box at the top of Google — "position zero."</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="schema-markup/"><strong>Schema Markup</strong></a> — Structured data that helps search engines and AI understand your page.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="e-e-a-t/"><strong>E-E-A-T</strong></a> — Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, Trust — Google's content-quality framework.</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Budgeting &amp; agency-buying terms</h2>
              <p>The terms that come up when you're budgeting for marketing or choosing an agency — what things cost, how engagements are structured, and how to judge lead quality.</p>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="cost-per-lead/"><strong>Cost Per Lead (CPL)</strong></a> — What you pay for one lead: total spend divided by leads generated.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="customer-acquisition-cost/"><strong>Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC)</strong></a> — Total sales + marketing cost per new customer; blended vs paid.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="mql-vs-sql/"><strong>MQL vs SQL</strong></a> — Marketing- vs sales-qualified leads, and why the handoff matters.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="marketing-retainer/"><strong>Marketing Retainer</strong></a> — A fixed monthly fee for an agreed ongoing scope, vs projects and hourly.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><a href="white-label-marketing/"><strong>White-Label Marketing</strong></a> — One agency delivers the work; another sells it under its own brand.</li></ul>
